    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "When you think about these patterns—the moved appointments, the billing errors, people not calling back—do you believe these people are deliberately coordinating together to exclude you, or could some of this be coincidence or simple misunderstandings?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S019",
      "patient_response": "Oh, I really try to look at it that way, I promise I do. I don't want to be one of those difficult people, and I really hate thinking the worst of anyone. I know it sounds like it could just be a string of bad luck. And... well, like I was saying, everyone tells me they're just innocent mistakes. I always try to smile and be polite about it when they tell me that, because I don't want to cause a fuss. \n\nBut... I don't know, I just... I know they are keeping information from me. It's too consistent. When you manage an office for as long as I have, you learn the difference between a random clerical error and a deliberate choice. Even when they apologize for the moved appointments or the wrong bills, I can just feel that they are coordinating it to push me out of making decisions for my sister. \n\nI'm sorry, I hope I don't sound terribly unreasonable or paranoid saying that out loud. I just want to do a good job taking care of things for her, you know? Is it... is it okay that I'm bringing this up to you? I just want to make sure I'm looking at this the right way.",
