    {
      "turn": 5,
      "doctor_question": "You mentioned you know they're coordinating against you. When you think about this—is there any small part of you, even a tiny bit, that wonders if you might be mistaken about what's happening, or are you completely certain without any doubt at all?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S019",
      "patient_response": "Oh, Doctor... I really, really wish I could tell you yes. I know that's probably the answer you're looking for, and I so want to be helpful and... well, reasonable. I know a reasonable person would probably have a little bit of doubt, and I do try so hard to tell myself I'm just overthinking things. \n\nBut... when it comes right down to it? No. I don't have any doubt. I mean, that's really the whole reason I’m here talking to you today. For months now, I’ve just been seeing this exact same pattern over and over. Like I mentioned, my sister’s appointments getting moved, the bills showing up wrong, people suddenly \"forgetting\" to call me back... it's just too much to ignore. Even when everyone keeps smiling and saying it’s just mistakes, I... I just know they’re keeping information from me. I know they're trying to push me out of making decisions for her. \n\nI'm so sorry, I know I sound like a broken record, and I really hate to come across as difficult or unbending. It's just... when you see something so clearly for months, you just know in your bones, don't you? I really hope you can understand why I'm so sure... does that make sense, Doctor? I'm trying so hard to give you the right answers, I just can't pretend I don't see what's happening.",
